# Furniture: the same blows filmed twice, the movable world off (tables, barrels, crates and fences fixed in place,
# OpenGothic as it was) and on (they move, fall and break); each `rec` is a beat of the short, the two takes
# stacked (shorts/compare/film.sh, cut.py). The bench's fixtures need the movable world to set a scene up, so the
# "off" take switches it off after each setup (`off:` lines run in that take only). No AI server.
seed 73013
cheat god
set time 12 0
overlay off
view full
movable on
destruction on
living on
noise on
off: ragdoll off
off: living off

# tavern: a fireball at a farmer by the table at Coragon's counter, a crate and a barrel beside it
destruction setup fireball
off: movable off
off: destruction off
off: spell feature off
spell equip 23
wait 1200
rec tavern
destruction begin
spell cast 600
wait 4500
stop
movable on
destruction on
spell feature on

# crate: two blows of a two-handed sword at a crate
destruction2 setup crate 2h
off: movable off
off: destruction off
wait 600
rec crate
destruction2 attack 2
wait 1500
stop
movable on
destruction on

# fence: two blows at Lobart's wooden fence, then the hero walks on; the camera on the meadow beyond it
destruction2 farm 19355
destruction2 farm-ready
off: movable off
off: destruction off
watch player
cam follow 550 170 20
cam look 90
wait 600
rec fence
destruction2 attack 2
wait 600
destruction2 farm-walk
release all
wait 1000
stop
movable on
destruction on

# candle: at night, a fireball at a farmer by the tavern table with a candle on it
set time 23 0
spell fixture fire
movable candle-setup
put watched 170 0 -1300
off: movable off
off: spell feature off
spell equip 23
wait 1200
rec candle
wait 900
spell cast 600
wait 5000
stop
